/**
 * HTTP SERVICE MAP
 * ------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Deterministic app-level HTTP service wiring by id.
 *
 * This file is the app-owned HTTP service map and has the highest
 * precedence for HTTP requests when service ids collide.
 *
 * Contract:
 *   - This file is only loaded in HTTP mode.
 *   - Keys are service ids accessed as $this->app->{id}.
 *   - Values may be:
 *       1) FQCN string
 *       2) ['class' => FQCN, 'options' => [...]]
 *   - Services are resolved as singletons per request.
 *   - Service constructors must follow:
 *       new Service(App $app, array $options = []).
 *
 * Effective HTTP precedence (services, left wins via PHP array union +):
 *   1) App HTTP services: /config/services_http.php
 *   2) App common services: /config/services.php
 *   3) Provider HTTP services: MAP_HTTP from registries listed in /config/providers.php
 *   4) Provider common services: MAP_COMMON from registries listed in /config/providers.php
 *   5) Vendor HTTP baseline: MAP_HTTP from citomni/http
 *
 * Policy:
 *   - Keep this file minimal.
 *   - Only declare HTTP-only app services or deliberate HTTP overrides.
 *   - Put services shared by HTTP and CLI in /config/services.php instead.
 *   - Do not mirror vendor or provider service maps here.
 *   - Keep definitions explicit and deterministic.
 *   - Pure data only. No logic, closures, factories, or side effects.
 *
 * Notes:
 *   - Order inside this array does not matter for resolution.
 *   - Duplicate keys in this file follow normal PHP array rules.
 *   - Invalid service classes or definitions should fail fast by design.
 */
return [

	/*
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	| Example: HTTP-only app service
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	*/
	// 'myHttpService' => \App\Http\Service\MyHttpService::class,

	/*
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	| Example: HTTP-only app service with options
	|--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	*/
	// 'myHttpServiceWithOptions' => [
	// 	'class' => \App\Http\Service\MyHttpService::class,
	// 	'options' => [
	// 		'example' => true,
	// 	],
	// ],

];
